## Valuation analysis

For each prime $\mathfrak{p}_i$ above 3, the residue field has characteristic 3, and $\bar{\omega}$ has order 671 (the 3-part collapses since $x^3 - 1 = (x-1)^3$ in char 3). Therefore:

$$v_{\mathfrak{p}_i}(1 - \omega^k) > 0 \iff 671 \mid k$$

**Case analysis for $v_{\mathfrak{p}_i}(S_a) = v_{\mathfrak{p}_i}(1-\omega^{a+1}) - v_{\mathfrak{p}_i}(1-\omega)$:**

Since $671 \nmid 1$, we have $v_{\mathfrak{p}_i}(1-\omega) = 0$ always.

